      "MOLLY: Look at that!\nBECKY: What?\nMOLLY: The prices. Regular for thirty- two cents a gallon, When's the last time you bought gas at that price?\nBECKY: Maybe there's a gas war on?",
      "MOLLY: . Who is it?\nBECKY: What's the matter with you?\nMOLLY: I heard something up there in the trees.\nBECKY: I don't hear anything.",
      "BECKY: She should have been back by now.\nMOLLY: I warned her. She probably got lost in the dark.\nBECKY: There's a light on -- maybe we should go see what's keeping her.\nMOLLY: I'm not moving.",
      "BECKY: Did you hear that?\nMOLLY: Uh-huh.\nMOLLY: See anything?\nBECKY: No.",
      "MOLLY: You ought to see your face. It's white as a sheet.\nBECKY: You scared the daylights out of me.\nMOLLY: We didn't hear your truck."
    ]
